# {{project_kebab}}

A [jenny](https://github.com/sashakm/jenny) service.

## Layout

Dependencies point inward. The domain depends on nothing external.

```
src/
  domain/          the hexagon — entities, value objects, events, the ports it owns
    model/         invariants enforced by types and smart constructors
    event/         domain event definitions, no dispatch
    port/          the outbound traits the domain owns
  application/     use cases — orchestration, and nothing else
  adapter/
    inbound/rest/  HTTP in: DTOs, TryFrom, status codes
    outbound/      the driven side: event publishing (stores are jenny's)
  lib.rs           the composition root, `build` — the only code that knows every layer
  main.rs          the binary: `build`, then run
```

## Running

```sh
just up      # development dependencies, if any
just run     # the service
{{#if persistence}}
just run-postgres   # the service, storing in the Postgres from `just up`
{{/if}}
{{#if graph}}
                    # (which has Apache AGE, for `postgres.graph(…)`)
{{/if}}
{{#if objects}}
just run-objects    # the service, with the S3-compatible store from `just up`
{{/if}}
just test
```

| Endpoint | |
|---|---|
| `GET /j/health/live` | is the process alive |
| `GET /j/health/ready` | should it get traffic |
| `GET /j/health/status` | what is mounted, and both versions |
| `GET /api/{{resource_plural}}` | the API |

With `server.management.address` set (see `config.yaml`), the `/j/…` endpoints move to
that port, at the same paths, and the API's port answers them with 404.

Listings accept `?page=`, `?page_size=`, repeatable `?sort=` (`field`, `-field`,
`field:desc`) and repeatable `?filter=` (`field:check:value`, checks `eq`, `begins`,
`ends`, `contains`, `gt`, `st`).

## Adding a resource

```sh
cargo jenny add resource order
```
